[{"id":"VRCE-2-67-1","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":1,"english":"Hearing of his father's death and the exile of his brothers, Bharata burning in grief, said these words.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.586,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067001","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"db7ca0abc9eeef5451179a29acf3cb5a95bb4f3cb584e48f68efe44f2fec8a48","compact":"e0f7700c758c6491f9e14c4653b7646a65fd04c71a58efa0453f5d508c314963","nasal":"e0f7700c758c6491f9e14c4653b7646a65fd04c71a58efa0453f5d508c314963"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-2","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":2,"english":"Deprived of my father as well as my brother like to a father, what shall I bewailing them and undone by you do with the kingdom?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.885,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067002","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4144f2fba503eccafc5d14ebdb87d66972b7708160f8b1bc130fea16bb207a0e","compact":"b7ee01cc0668ea7b20dc9200813cd3b87008609a65f3cce545c69c712ba04064","nasal":"b7ee01cc0668ea7b20dc9200813cd3b87008609a65f3cce545c69c712ba04064"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-3","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":3,"english":"You, like one throwing alkali on a sore, have, by bringing about the death of the king and making Rāma an ascetic, heaped grief on grief.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067003","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cff81677085ac274a36a51843591bb10dc361aa2bc20109c9b942148833fc7a7","compact":"1bd792374a9dcfd98e2f8bbcc87c17980d2b7d7df6b0017ca22a6d11b92c035e","nasal":"1bd792374a9dcfd98e2f8bbcc87c17980d2b7d7df6b0017ca22a6d11b92c035e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-4","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":4,"english":"You have come like the fatal night for the destruction of this race. Not under-standing it, my father embraced live coal.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067004","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9f9098888f5cae755e8891ffb78955013f170039da457b7a0e2b6b26d14b46c2","compact":"d8fb358391b73bb46c9af8f5b916eba2b050c1042b448dff2c3380058e4980f3","nasal":"984788cfaabe5cadd6589a8a2595ff9d84626011efa4181fc570c021eb59e43f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-5","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":5,"english":"Afflicted with grief for their son, even if Kausalya and Sumitrā live, it will be hard for them to do so in the presence of you, my mother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.952,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067005","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ccc551cc5d15d3442ec74c2b6d2f55410cac6b559d574a84ea99a309dcceca71","compact":"e282a661265855e82afacbd33f78dcdccfca413dd9e4ce296753578a1fad4173","nasal":"e282a661265855e82afacbd33f78dcdccfca413dd9e4ce296753578a1fad4173"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-6","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":6,"english":"Surely the noble and virtuous Råma, well knowing his duties towards his superiors, regards you as highly as he does his own mother.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.843,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067006","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"63388761655d9089b4fd8c2157d65ac77c04215f82d51f7e88fe86f5bff5cb51","compact":"fb1c6f1f1155cb6bed7eeac82e713f67633de4e380d76c5b2001d4f8510505ee","nasal":"fb1c6f1f1155cb6bed7eeac82e713f67633de4e380d76c5b2001d4f8510505ee"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-7","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":7,"english":"In the same way, my eldest mother, the farsighted Kausalyā, doing her duties by you, bears herself like a sister.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067007","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bcb754b477d716546a71abaac7235caf3ac1fde063b9eb8af3d7bef086404ca6","compact":"01d8f86fb818ea91a0fbc766800fffe86e2218b4f1de664eb684b3ac947d4729","nasal":"01d8f86fb818ea91a0fbc766800fffe86e2218b4f1de664eb684b3ac947d4729"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-8","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":8,"english":"Why, O sinful one, having sent to the woods her magnanimous son, clad in bark, do you not grieve?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.814,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067008","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"863764f82f4d370209ed654b6ed9f2e0219f83e6c9a5d9c6691597303fdcb2c7","compact":"9ef89aada5c670d2b5493020a87d7e78031a888194ad91282e78afdfd43afc27","nasal":"7d120b05b5f33bca7e5b44218dfa4f7ab807b1cf99ca23a66e2289e00e1a8e37"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-9","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":9,"english":"Having exiled the famous and heroic Rāma seeing no sin, clad in bark, what benefit do you perceive as yours?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067009","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2ef2c2e6a49b68387bf62786ce04174a046b6a184f361682e93e876e13f6348c","compact":"aa888c44aea126c629545ad85a66bf4062f8cdabfe1cb872f0a262df44de8d3c","nasal":"b41b6f3e8ad963b43f44eab4747a9ebc4fdde2301917983d7293aeeb803b0ef0"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-10","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":10,"english":"I deem that you did not know how very highly I regarded Rāghava; and therefore it is that you have brought this mighty calamity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.688,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067010","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2b7c5c70eff8d2f2cc810df5068bfd23168a4e1ffdb74a0b78ab1dbab9ba9bae","compact":"198994af459a2bb91ab4f32fc1b6351efac2185689d9047de531b8adc944bc16","nasal":"198994af459a2bb91ab4f32fc1b6351efac2185689d9047de531b8adc944bc16"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-11","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":11,"english":"Not seeing those chiefs of men, Rāma and Lakşmaņa, by virtue of whose energy can I venture to rule the kingdom?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.877,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067011","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b2cbf7db0d0822e152364b7e9ce186eab2f56f8b61ba7aae2b43b6db8a6ee48d","compact":"3e9053d26fcbb6f22773ae62c64ac97945a07f62983680b24aaa40e7103760e3","nasal":"3e9053d26fcbb6f22773ae62c64ac97945a07f62983680b24aaa40e7103760e3"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-12","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":12,"english":"The monarch was ever protected by that powerful one possessed of mighty energy, as Meru is protected by its forest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.623,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067012","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"104fbfea10eb044a9aadf8879b12c093abd0b5b1183f5306b04ab370b1a1fff5","compact":"ef61187dde144ef6a993a64c0bba6a6f61a4310f26ca103007d3475fe90308e3","nasal":"ea2c6e829c9776ed94512a1d4944fd4d5a4a4f233bdef45f32184357a2e6c73e"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-13","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":13,"english":"Like a calf burdened with a load capable of being borne by a mighty ox, by what energy shall I bear this burden which was borne by an exceedingly strong person?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067013","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cf1c160e2d68297621626ca91da6ecaed4a1a185a1e5d2cb26edf8ff3f964da3","compact":"b4514cad1e00eac213d83e98dbe0c65b1469f79dd1cd7b8c14ed658845f18179","nasal":"b4514cad1e00eac213d83e98dbe0c65b1469f79dd1cd7b8c14ed658845f18179"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-14","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":14,"english":"And even if this strength be mine through yoga or vigour of intellect, I will not crown with success the hopes of you, proud of your son.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.635,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-73-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2067014","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"69f81c2aad7a093995eb42866a29ece9b3897bd1e2fa716835565a7428541a75","compact":"c434736405be48c3b00611fbde9fa87d65f2465e298454a3d9da32f94852265d","nasal":"c434736405be48c3b00611fbde9fa87d65f2465e298454a3d9da32f94852265d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-67-15","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":67,"verse":15,"english":"The high-souled Bharata afflicted (his mother) with multitudes of words causing pain; and distressed with grief, emitted sounds like to a lion in the cave of Mandāra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1",